 "format": "Commander",
 "name": "The Vision and Scarlet Witch: Chaos Magic",
 "notes": [
  "Plan: the commander adds {R} and gets a +1/+1 counter whenever you cast a spell. One-mana red spells are free and two-mana spells cost one, so a hand of cheap spells turns into a large flier and a pile of triggers in one turn.",
  "Why mono-red works here: the commander is the mana engine. The deck needs cheap spells and ways to keep drawing them, and red has both.",
  "Card flow that keeps the chain going: Wiccan, Young Avenger (exile and play the top card on every noncreature spell), Hex Magic, Reckless Impulse, Wrenn's Resolve, Light Up the Stage, Asgardian Inspiration, Heroes' Hangout, Wanda's Vision.",
  "Nico Minoru deals 2 to each opponent whenever you cast a spell from anywhere other than your hand, and most of the card flow above plays cards from exile.",
  "Ways to win: commander damage in the air (Team Tactics or Temur Battle Rage for double strike), Guttersnipe, Firebrand Archer, Kessig Flamebreather, Electrostatic Field and Thermo-Alchemist pinging per spell, Grapeshot, and Photon Blast Barrage.",
  "The commander is an artifact creature, so Vandalblast from an opponent and artifact removal both hit it. Lightning Greaves and Swiftfoot Boots are the protection.",
  "Ownership tags on each card: have = confirmed owned; freed = from a deck folded Nov 16 or a precon cut; likely = Marvel common or uncommon, or your staples pile; check = owned but maybe sleeved elsewhere; buy = not known to be owned. Several of the spell payoffs are also in the Gandalf deck.",
  "Buy list (Nov 12 snapshot): about $30 for the 31 buy cards, most of them under $1. Estimated, not simulated: wins around turns 8-10, faster with a full hand and the commander surviving a turn.",
  "Bracket 2 check: 0 Game Changers, no extra turns, no land destruction, no tutors, no rituals. Past in Flames plus a long chain can end a game in one turn; mention it at a new table."
 ],
 "order": 6.3,
